\id 2TH - Open English Translation—Readers’ Version (OET-RV) v0.2.2
\usfm 3.0
\ide UTF-8
\h 2 Thessalonians
\toc1 Paul’s second letter to the believers in Thessalonica
\toc2 2 Thessalonians
\mt2 Paul’s second letter to the believers in
\mt1 Thessalonica
\rem This is still an early look into the unpolished text of the Open English Translation of the Bible. Please double-check the text in advance before using in public.
\c 1
\p
\v 1 \add This letter is from\add* Paul, Silas, and Timothy.
\p \add It’s written\add* to the assembly of \add believers\add* in God our father and \add the\add* master Jesus Messiah \add there\add* in Thessalonica.
\p
\v 2 \add May\add* God our father and \add the\add* master Jesus Messiah give grace and peace to all of you.
\s1 Paul’s thanking and praying
\p
\v 3 We should be always thanking God for you brothers and sisters, and it’s right that we do, because your faith is growing and you all \add display\add* plenty of love towards each other.
\v 4 That’s why we boast about you all in God’s assemblies, because of your endurance and faith \add despite\add* the persecutions \add you encounter\add* and the tribulations that you put up with.
\s1 The Judgement after Jesus’s return
\p
\v 5 That shows God’s righteous judgement in that you’re considered worthy \add to enter\add* God’s kingdom because of what you’ve \add had to\add* suffer.
\v 6 God is righteous, and he’s \add the one who\add* will repay those who oppress you and make life difficult for you all,
\v 7 then all of you who’ve been oppressed will be able to relax when the master Jesus comes back from heaven with his powerful army.
\v 8 With a fiery flame he’ll judge those who don’t know God and those who haven’t accepted the good message of our master Jesus Messiah.
\v 9 They’ll be sentenced to eternal destruction—banished from Yahweh’s presence and from the display of his strength
\v 10 when he’s honoured by his righteous followers and admired by those who believe in him just as you believed our testimony to all of you.
\p
\v 11 We’re also praying all the time for you all that you’ll be considered worthy of our god’s calling and will live out your good intentions and demonstrate your faith with power,
\v 12 so that the reputation of our master Jesus will be honoured in you all, and you in him, thanks to the grace of our God and of \add the\add* master Jesus Messiah.
\c 2
\s1 The false man-God
\p
\v 1 Now concerning the \add return\add* of our master Jesus Messiah and our being gathered together with him, we are asking you all, brothers and sisters,
\v 2 to not be alarmed or have your thinking jolted \add back-and-forth\add* by any ‘spirit’ or message or letter that seems to come from us that tries to say that the master \add has already returned\add*.
\v 3 Don’t let anyone deceive you in any way, because before that happens \add many people will turn away from the good message\add*, and the lawless man will be revealed—the \add conveyor\add* of destruction
\v 4 who opposes every god or object of worship and puts himself above them all—seating himself in God’s temple and demonstrating that he is God.
\p
\v 5 Don’t you remember how I told you \add people\add* this when I was still with you?
\v 6 Now you know what’s restraining \add him\add* so that he’ll be revealed at the \add proper\add* time,
\v 7 because the mystery of lawlessness is already at work, except that it’s being restrained until he’s taken out of the middle,
\v 8 and then the lawless \add man\add* will be revealed. The master Jesus will kill him with his breath and neutralise him with the appearance of his coming.
\v 9 \add The lawless man\add* was coming and working \add under\add* Satan with his power and signs and false miracles
\v 10 and with every unrighteous seduction. These deceive those who are perishing, because they never had the love for the truth that could have saved them.
\v 11 That’s why God is sending deceptive practices to them, so that they can \add continue to\add* believe in the falsehood,
\v 12 so that all of those who didn’t believe in the truth, but took pleasure in \add wicked actions\add*, will be judged \add and sentenced\add*.
\s1 Keep hold of the truth
\p
\v 13 But brothers and sisters, we \add here\add* should always be thanking God for you who were loved by Yahweh. From the beginning God chose you for salvation in the holiness of \add the\add* spirit and faith \add in\add* the truth
\v 14 which he called you to. That was through the good message that we \add brought\add* so that you might obtain the \add power\add* that \add comes from\add* our master Jesus Messiah.
\v 15 So as a result, brothers and sisters, stand firm and keep hold of the practices that we taught you—whether it was spoken or written in our letters.
\p
\v 16 May our master Messiah Jesus and God our father who loved us and gives us eternal comfort, and by his grace gives good hope,
\v 17 comfort your minds and strengthen you all in everything you do and every good message \add you share\add*.
\c 3
\s1 Pray for us as well
\p
\v 1 The other thing, brothers and sisters, is to keep praying for us, so that the master’s message will keep spreading and being honoured, just like it was among you,
\v 2 and so that we might escape from the schemes of perverse and evil people, because not everyone believes \add this message\add*.
\v 3 But the master is faithful and will strengthen you all and will keep you from the evil one.
\v 4 We are confident that with Yahweh’s \add help\add*, you are following all of our instructions and will continue to do so.
\p
\v 5 May the master direct your thoughts towards God’s love and Messiah’s endurance.
\s1 The warning against laziness
\p
\v 6 Brothers and sisters, we’re instructing you to avoid those who are only lazily living out their faith, and not following the practices that they were taught by us.
\v 7 You yourselves know that it’s appropriate to be imitating us, because we didn’t loaf when we were among you all,
\v 8 nor did we eat food from anyone that we didn’t deserve, but we worked even when it was hard—day and night, so that we wouldn’t be a burden on anybody,
\v 9 not that we didn’t have the right, but in order to make ourselves a \add good\add* example that you could emulate.
\v 10 Even when we were \add there\add* with you, \add brothers and sisters,\add* we instructed you that anyone who’s not willing to work doesn’t \add deserve\add* to eat.
\p
\v 11 \add Yes,\add* we’ve heard that there are some who associate with you, \add brothers and sisters,\add* who are lazy—not doing any work, but \add just\add* meddling,
\v 12 so we’re instructing those people, and urging them by \add the authority of\add* \add the\add* master Jesus Messiah, to \add just\add* quietly get down to work, and then they’ll have food to eat.
\v 13 But \add the rest of\add* you, brothers and sisters, don’t get discouraged from doing good.
\p
\v 14 And if there’s anyone \add there\add* who won’t submit to the contents of this letter, then take note of that person and don’t associate with them, in order that they might be persuaded.
\v 15 Don’t consider them as an enemy, but reprimand them like you would reprimand a brother or sister.
\s1 Farewell
\p
\v 16 May the master of peace himself give all of you peace through everyone and in every way. \add May\add* the master be with all of you.
\p
\v 17 \sig This farewell is in my own handwriting—I’m Paul, and I do this with every letter I write.\sig*
\p
\v 18 \sig \+add May\+add* the grace from our master Jesus Messiah be with all of you.\sig*
